WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.880
A siren races down the street towards you,

2
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:05.300
passes, and speeds away.

3
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.720
Just as it passes, you
hear its pitch drop.

4
00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:13.210
Yet the siren itself sends out
one steady note the whole time.

5
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.230
Nothing on board has changed.

6
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.490
So why does a passing siren drop in pitch?

7
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:22.150
And what can that shift tell
us about how fast it moves?

8
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.790
In this mission, you'll draw
the waves from a moving source,

9
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.570
each one spreading out from where
the source was when it left.

10
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.240
Then you'll find out how
big the shift can be,

11
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:34.920
and what it reveals about speed.

12
00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:39.550
Your mission: explain the drop in pitch,
and what it can tell us about speed.
